step-by-step walkthroughs, which lets

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:43.760
you see exactly where to click and it

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.240
moves you through each step as you go.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:48.280
So, take back your time and skip the

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:50.480
busy work. Go to scribe.house/holsagted

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:52.240
to get started for free. But anyway,

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.720
back to the video and onto the next

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:57.280
step, which is this. I used AI to both

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.120
edit my draft novel and polish it to

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:02.520
turn it into a print-ready novel. Yep.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:04.200
So, first up in my editing process, I

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:06.280
actually chose to extend the book and

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:08.680
make it bigger because my first draft

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:10.440
came out to be just 40,000 words and

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:13.560
most mystery books I see sell well on

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:15.440
Amazon are about 50,000 words or more.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:17.320
Claude asked me some questions on which

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:19.360
parts I wanted to expand on and then

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:21.400
that was it. It just worked its magic.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:24.200
It took about 20 minutes to do this as

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:26.240
this was quite intense work. It extended

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:28.560
the chapters and even added two new

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:31.920
chapters as well taking it to just over

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:33.880
50,000 words, which was perfect. Now I

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.080
needed to check for errors. So to do

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:38.280
that I use two different AI chatbots,

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.320
ChatGPT and Google's Gemini, to

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:42.400
basically act as third-party neutral

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:44.600
editors. I uploaded my manuscript to

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:46.280
them and I got each to read over it to

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.440
see if they could spot any mistakes or

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:50.760
continuity errors. And because I wrote

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:53.400
this book in tandem with Claude and I

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:55.240
read over each chapter as I wrote it and

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:57.320
I got it to fix up mistakes along the

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:59.360
way, there were actually very few

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:02.000
errors. Although they did spot some

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:04.320
which frankly, even in a human written

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:06.400
novel, you'd expect. Then I came back to

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.080
Claude and with Opus still turned on, I

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:10.960
copied and pasted in the errors that

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:13.040
ChatGPT and Gemini found in a fresh chat

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:15.520
along with a copy of the manuscript and

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:17.800
I let Claude do its AI magic. And in

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:21.360
just six minutes, it went through and

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:23.680
fixed them all up. Nice. So, after I

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:26.560
downloaded this new draft, there was one

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:29.200
final big thing I needed to do and that

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:31.400
was polishing. So I started a new chat

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:34.000
in our book project and I uploaded this

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:36.400
final draft and I asked the Opus version

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:39.280
of Claude to polish it up and to turn it

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:41.960
into a final manuscript that is fun and

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:44.760
easy to read. And this definitely took a

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:47.080
little while, obviously I sped it up,

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:49.320
but in total it took roughly 15 minutes

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:52.800
for it to do this. But it was well worth

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:56.080
it because at the end, I had my AI

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:58.920
mystery novel that was, well, actually

00:12:56.080 --> 00:13:00.280
good. So then, this is the final copy

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.640
that you will want to read over to

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:04.839
double-check for any You can do what I

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:06.400
did and pop it into a Google Doc to turn

00:13:04.839 --> 00:13:09.360
it into a document that you can edit

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:11.480
yourself. But before I could upload it,

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:14.240
there was something else I needed to do.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:16.880
I now needed to make a book cover and AI

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:19.080
has, surprise, surprise, actually made

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:21.240
this pretty easy. So for this, I used

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:23.200
two tools. The first was Nana Banana,

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:25.040
Google's AI image generator, which I

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:27.360
access through Google's all-in-one media

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:29.200
generation platform called Flow. And I

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:31.560
also used my favorite AI powered

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.160
graphics editing app, Canva. And

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.480
seriously, when it comes to making a

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:37.800
book cover, I really wouldn't overthink

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:39.760
it. Like, this is a top-selling murder

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:42.080
mystery book, and as you can see, the

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:44.400
cover is pretty simple, isn't it? But,

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:47.320
it gives the right vibe, which for this

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:49.480
style of book is cute and cozy. So, it's

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:52.160
the vibe that's most important here.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.840
But, either way, I started out by coming

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:56.040
to Google Flow. If you don't have an

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:57.760
account yet, that's easy. You can scroll

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.880
down to pricing and sign up for either

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:01.800
the free account or the pro account with

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:03.480
their free 30-day trial. Then, once

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.480
logged in, I clicked to create a new

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:07.480
project. And then, in the chat settings,

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:09.920
I switched to the image generation. And

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:11.960
I selected to create a 3x4 image. And I

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:13.560
chose to generate four images. And I

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:15.680
also picked my favorite Nana Banana

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:18.040
model, which is pro. Then, I just typed

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:20.160
in a prompt explaining what I wanted my

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.360
book cover to contain and what image

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:24.680
style I wanted it in. And then, that was

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:26.760
it. Nana Banana went ahead and made four

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:28.640
images for me. I also went ahead and

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:31.080
generated a bunch more just to get

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:33.320
myself lots of options to pick from. And

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:35.480
out of these, this one was my favorite.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:37.600
But, I needed to make some tweaks. So, I

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:39.320
prompted it telling it what to change,

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:41.040
and it made the changes for me. And

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:44.080
then, once I'd finished tweaking it, I

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:46.960
just downloaded it, upscaled to 2K. And

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:48.720
yes, before anyone asks, all images made

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:51.160
in Flow with the pro account currently,

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:53.640
as of me filming, have no watermark,

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.640
which is super handy. Then, next I came

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:57.600
to Canva. You can use the free version

00:14:55.640 --> 00:15:00.000
of this, but I used the pro version to

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.480
get access to more fonts and to upscale

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.640
my book cover into higher resolution.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:06.800
So, if you do want to sign up for a free

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.520
30-day trial to it, I'll include my

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:10.760
affiliate link in the description.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:14.360
Either way, I started a new project and

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:16.520
set it to be 1,600 by 2,560

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:18.760
pixels, which is the standard Kindle

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:20.560
ebook size. And I uploaded the image of

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:22.400
my book cover and placed it in the

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.440
middle. Then, I came to elements and

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:26.760
selected shapes from the menu and added

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.760
a rectangle and I drag and dropped it to

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:30.840
fill the empty top section and I

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:32.960
selected a matching color from the color

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:35.800
picker. Then I came to the text menu and

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:37.920
elements and I added in my top tagline

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:40.280
and then I switched the tagline font.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:43.600
Now, as you can see, Canva, especially

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:45.120
the pro version, has lots of fonts, but

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:46.960
if you have a font you want to use in

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:48.960
particular, you can just type in the

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.880
name of it and select it. Then after

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:53.240
that, I came to the text effects menu

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.960
and selected a fun effect and for this I

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:57.080
thought the echo effect worked well with

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:58.800
it. So, once I had it looking the way

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.720
that I wanted, I clicked on advanced

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:02.680
text settings and then I used the slider

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:04.640
to decrease the letter spacing for the

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:07.000
tagline. And then, that was pretty much

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:08.840
it. I just repeated the process, but I

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.720
added it at the bottom with the author

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:12.280
name. And then, when I had it looking

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:14.960
the way that I wanted, I just clicked

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:17.120
share, download and I changed it to JPEG

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:19.240
and I upscaled the image quality as high

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:21.240
as it could go and I just clicked

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:23.520
download. And now I have my own Kindle

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:25.520
book cover. Yay. And also, just a quick

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:27.760
note, I unfortunately only have time in

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:30.080
this video to show how to upload novels

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:32.560
as ebooks, but if you'd like to use

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:35.080
Amazon's KDP program to also sell your

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:36.960
novels as print-on-demand books, you can

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:39.040
use the book cover template generator to

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:41.160
download a template that you can use to

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:43.800
create a print-ready book cover to sell

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:46.040
as an actual physical book, too. So

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:48.080
then, after I had my cover, I then moved

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:51.480
on to the next step, turning my story

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:52.920
into a Kindle ready file. So, first up,

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:55.080
what I did was I came back to my chat

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:57.160
thread with Claude Opus and I asked it

00:16:55.080 --> 00:17:00.120
to format my book manuscript into a

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:02.480
nice, easy-to-read Kindle friendly file,

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:04.480
which it did. So, I went ahead and I

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:06.439
downloaded this. Then I came to Amazon's

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:08.040
free software, Kindle Create, and I

00:17:06.439 --> 00:17:09.880
downloaded it and installed it on my

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:12.079
computer and then I opened it up,

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:14.240
started a new file and uploaded the

00:17:12.079 --> 00:17:17.160
newly formatted novel that Claude made

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:18.800
for me using the reflowable book format.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.920
And when I did, it asked me which

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:23.000
chapters or sections to include. And

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:24.640
then, honestly, that was pretty much it.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.760
Because Claude had already formatted the

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:29.120
document for Kindle, it looked great as

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:31.000
is. I just made one change. You can add

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.000
text or change the formatting on any of

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:34.680
the pages that you like. So, I just

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.360
added in an author name to the front

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.840
page. And then I clicked to preview it

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:40.400
to double-check how it would look on a

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:42.480
tablet. And as you can see, again, it

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:44.280
looks pretty much perfect. So, I just

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:47.760
went ahead and clicked export and saved

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:50.000
it as a KPF file. Nice. So, then, the

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:51.960
moment of truth had come. It was now

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:54.640
time to upload and set my ebook to

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:56.760
publish on Amazon's Kindle marketplace,

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:59.080
while also optimizing it for free

00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:00.800
traffic. So, first of all, I signed into

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:03.440
my account that I already had for

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:05.800
Amazon's self-publishing service, KDP,

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:07.880
and it's free for anybody to go in there

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:10.160
and create an account. Then, once I was

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:11.680
logged in, I clicked to add a new book.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:13.600
And then, on the screen, I needed to

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:15.120
choose which book type to make. So, if

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:16.560
I'd wanted to add in a physical

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:18.520
print-on-demand book, I could have

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:20.640
chosen either a hardcover or a

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:23.160
paperback. But since I'm uploading an

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:25.600
ebook, I chose that. Then next, I needed

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:27.280
to add a book title and a book subtitle.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:29.920
And this is actually an opportunity to

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:31.600
optimize it for free traffic. So, as I

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.440
mentioned earlier, we can optimize it

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:35.520
for search engines, especially if you

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:37.960
picked a low-competition niche. This is

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:40.000
called SEO. But we can also optimize it

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:42.640
for GEO, which is generative engine

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:45.040
optimization traffic. Basically, this is

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.760
the AI recommendation feed. Essentially,

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:49.280
if you open up Kindle, and inside of the

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:51.240
website and app, Amazon's AI algorithm

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:53.120
will choose and recommend books to you.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:56.320
And a well-known quirk is that the new

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:58.200
books seem to get a 30-day algorithmic

00:18:56.320 --> 00:19:00.400
boost. So, this can be a great source of

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:02.560
free traffic to get initial sales and

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:04.560
reviews. So, what I did was I asked

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:07.160
Claude to help me write this, while also

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:09.440
noting who my target audience is. And it

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.240
came back with three options for me. And

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:13.640
out of these, I liked option two the

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:16.280
most. So, I copied it and then I pasted

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:18.920
it back in on the KDP submission form.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:21.040
Then next up, I decided to not create a

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:23.280
series yet because it's probably not

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:25.560
worth it until you have a second book,

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:27.600
you know? Then in the author section,

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:30.080
you can enter in your name or if you

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:32.320
want, you can use a pen name. Amazon

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:34.040
doesn't mind either way. Then after

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:36.680
that, I scrolled down to the description

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:38.600
box and of course, at this point I

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:40.600
switched back to Claude and I asked it

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:43.560
to not only create a description

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:45.840
optimized for SEO and GEO traffic, but

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:48.440
to write a description designed to hook

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:50.240
readers in from the very first sentence.

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:52.400
And then I copied the optimized

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:55.240
description it gave me and I pasted it

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:57.520
into Amazon's KDP and then after ticking

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:59.720
I own the rights and that it didn't have

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:02.480
any explicit content, I came to

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:04.640
categories. And here you can categorize

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:07.280
your book into three categories. Your

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:09.480
first category is your primary category,

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:11.200
so I chose the one that best fits it.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:13.160
Then after that, I came to the book

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:15.560
keywords section and I asked Claude to

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:17.760
come up with seven keywords for me. And

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:19.440
while I liked six of them, I noticed

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:22.360
that one of the sets of keywords it came

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:24.320
up with involved author names. Anything

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:27.280
involving names, trademarks, or

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:29.680
copyrights is something I stay clear of.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:32.080
So I asked Claude to redo this avoiding

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:34.800
these and it made that change for me, no

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:37.080
problem. So I copied these keywords and

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:38.960
I pasted them back into my book listing.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:41.280
And then while you can choose to set the

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:43.640
book as a pre-order, I set it to release

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:45.200
now. Then on the next page, I just

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:47.400
scrolled down and uploaded my book

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:49.040
manuscript I made with Kindle Create.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:51.120
And then I scrolled down and uploaded my

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.960
book cover that I made with Canva. And

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:55.480
then I scrolled down again and gave a

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:58.360
full disclosure of the AI content in my

00:20:55.480 --> 00:21:00.600
book. Amazon has publicly said that this

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:02.480
is just for their own internal data.

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:04.520
They don't release this publicly and

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:07.240
they don't penalize books that are AI

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:09.920
written. So I think it would be wise to

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:12.040
disclose honestly here. Then I scrolled

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:13.960
down to accessibility, disclosed I

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:16.400
wasn't quite sure on how accessible my

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:18.280
book was, which was fine. Then I went

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:20.200
over to the next page, pricing. I

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:22.280
enrolled in the Kindle Select program,

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:25.000
and I chose to have a higher 70%

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:26.800
royalty, which is what most authors do.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:29.800
For that, your book needs to be priced

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:32.240
at at least $3. Most ebooks I see in

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:34.360
this niche priced at around $5, so

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:35.960
that's what I did, too. And then, that

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:38.400
was it. The book was ready to either be

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:40.760
published or, as I did, to save it as a

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:42.360
draft ready to be published later. And

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:44.200
check it out. While I did choose to

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:46.440
break up the steps into little micro

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:49.320
tasks spread out over multiple days,

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:52.040
when I timed how long each task took,

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:54.640
and ended it up, combined, it came out

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:58.040
to just under 3 hours from start to

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:59.760
finish. Very cool. So then, if you'd

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:02.040
like to learn about other business ideas

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:03.600
that people are starting with AI tools,

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:05.560
be sure to watch my next video here on

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:08.080
screen, and I will see you in the next

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:08.080
video.

